Primitive deep well {1..12,182}: t*=14/183=[0;13,14]. The two best rationals flanking t*:
  t=1/13: min_v||v t|| = 0/13, killed by v=182 (13|182=True)   [CF convergent 1/13 (needs 13|v)]
  t=1/14: min_v||v t|| = 0/14, killed by v=182 (14|182=True)   [mediant 1/14 (needs 14|v)]

=> far element = lcm(13,14) = 182 blocks BOTH. CF descent EXPLAINS 182, but delivers
